A||||7||Brandon86SE||Dash Lights||||5||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||08-15-2001||09:33 PM||||Alright, I have a problem, and it's been bugging me for too long, and I need to fix it.  My dash (gauge) lights will not come on when my lights are on.  This makes for obvious problems with night driving.  My indicator (shift up, signal, check engine, etc.) lights work fine.  I checked all the appropriate fuses, and everything's fine.  I have heard of some people having problems like this after installing a stereo, and I do have an aftermarket stereo.  However, today I totally unplugged it, and the lights were still out.  I know that the bulbs are fine, 'cause the weirdest part of this problem is that sometimes they come back, often for a couple months, but now they're out again.  I checked the dimmer switch, and everything seems to be fine, it isn't corroded out, and the overhead lights do come on when it is turned all the way up.  If anyone has seen anything like this in the past, or have any suggestions please let me know.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-15-2001||09:36 PM||||Check and clean the ground hook-up on the rear of the panel.<BR>If that doesn't work, splice into it and run a secondary ground for that side of the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||08-15-2001||10:23 PM||||Actually as a follow up, I forgot to mention that it isn't just the dash lights.  The lights on the AC/Heater panel are also out, and the backlighting for the oil pressure/ battery gauges too.  Basically, all the Orange lighting.  The radio works fine, and lights up fine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||08-15-2001||10:31 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012226.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012226.html</A> <P>I had just fixed my lights a couple days ago.  Took off the whole console and looked at the back of the cluster.  The problem with my lights is that the little connectors for the bulb sockets are not making good connections to the copper on the circuit.  I bent up the connectors and made sure they were all in place and they all worked....  for a day.  Now my tach lights are out <I>again</I>.  I'm now trying to find something that I can use to repair the copper circuit.  Anyone have any ideas??<P>Did you try taking off the back of the cluster?  It's just 5 torx screws and two small screws on the bottom.  Try pressing up against the circuit and the bulbs and jiggle the wiring while your lights are turned on and see if anything happens.<P>I've found that if just <B>one</B> bulb is out of whack that strange things can happen to the rest of the gauges... like my temp gauge problem (which is fine now).||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||08-15-2001||10:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B>Actually as a follow up, I forgot to mention that it isn't just the dash lights.  The lights on the AC/Heater panel are also out, and the backlighting for the oil pressure/ battery gauges too.  Basically, all the Orange lighting.  The radio works fine, and lights up fine.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK.  Ignore my previous post then.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Max The Chainsaw||08-15-2001||10:40 PM||||You mught want to check the dash light transistor. It sounds like all the lights you have out are the ones controlled by the dimmer circuit. The dimmer control for the lights doesn't operate the lights directly but controls a transistor that operates the lights.  It is located under the dash, behind the cluster above the throttle pedal. It's mounted on a 2 inch square aluminum heat sink. <P>A replacement should be easy to locate as just about every GM car made during the 80's had one of these under the dash. I went to the salvage yard when mine went bad and came home with about 8 of em in an hour.<P>Greg<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Max The Chainsaw (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||JamesWM83||08-15-2001||11:19 PM||||I just started having this problem too damn it. I have my stereo installed and my amp.. and all my dash lights worked fine after installin these thing last night. tonight the wouldn't work. On the way home the flickered on then off again.. and now I cnat get them back on. Someone please help me out to what this problem could be. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>~James<P>1986 Fiero GT! <BR>2.8 4 clicker. White face guages, blue backlighting, grey marlbe dash kit, IRM sie rocker scoops, fierostore.com 1/4 window scoop, V8 Archie Warber hood, rear added sway bar, silver mesh inserts in tail-lights, mesh inserts in turn lamp and grill, KYB shocks and struts, Eibach lowering springs, 300 watt amp, and 600 watt 12" sub, clarion pro audio 5x6" plates, Kenwood Xcelon 4x10's, clarion pro audio cd player, monster calbe wiring, rockford wiring, pheonix gold wiring, chrome ocelot exhaust tips||||reg||1
Z||000007||Brandon86SE||08-15-2001||11:47 PM||||Ok, Max, that sounds like the most likely problem is what you have listed, since it is everything on the dimmer switch.  I just ran down to the garage to take a look over the gas pedal, and didn't see a transistor there.  Do I actually have to remove the dash to get at it, or should I be able to see it and get at it without?||||reg||1
